V1  IS THE CHANGE OF REFERENCE ANGLE AN AUTOMORPHISM OF g ?
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V1  count: bracket pairs on which Psi(beta) fails to be an automorphism = 0
V1  count: departures of Psi from a one-parameter group, Psi(b)Psi(c) = Psi(b+c) = 0
V1  count: departures of Psi from orthogonality = 0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V2  THE GENERATOR D
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V2  D sends v1 -> {0, -1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0} and v4 -> {0, 0, 0, 0, -1, 0, 0}
V2  count: Leibniz failures of D (0 confirms D is a derivation of g) = 0
V2  solutions X of ad_X = D : {}
V2  count: inner solutions (0 confirms D is an OUTER derivation) = 0
V2  why: v1 and v2 are central in g, so ad_X(v1) = 0 for every X, while D(v1) = -v2.
V2  count: departures of ad_X(v1) from 0 for a general X = 0
V2  count: departures of D from antisymmetry, D* = -D (needed for Thm 8.7) = 0
V2  count: departures of D from -ad_{v7} on span{v4,v5,v7} = 0
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V3  THE EXTENDED BRACKET
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V3  count: departures of [v0, v_a] from theta0'(t) D(v_a), a = 1..7 = 0
V3  this holds for an ARBITRARY smooth theta0(t); no constancy is used.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V4  CLOSURE
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
V4  the structure functions carrying the index 0 are the entries of theta0'(t) D,
    so the span is a Lie algebra iff theta0' is constant, and is then the
    semidirect product  R (x)_{w D} g,  w = theta0'.
V4  count: departures of the w-uniform bracket from the semidirect product = 0
V4  count: departures of R (x)_{wD} g from R^2 (+) se(2) (+) se(2), A = -(v0+w v7)/w = 0
